@startuml implementation-issue-agent-starts
' cumin works - states of an implementation issue: which transitions start an agent,
' which of them read the quota usage first, and what cumin does while it stops after the current runs.
' The states and the transitions are the ones of implementation-issue-states.puml; only the names are shown.
' Render: run scripts/render-diagrams.sh at the root of the repository.

hide empty description

state "Draft (no status label)" as Draft
state "ready" as Ready
state "implementing" as Implementing
state "checking" as Checks
state "reviewing" as Reviewing
state "awaiting-merge-decision" as OwnerReview
state "merging" as Merging
Merging : do / cumin sends the merge (also while cumin stops)
state "awaiting-decision" as Decision

[*] --> Draft
Draft -[#888888,dashed]-> Ready : the Owner adds ready
Ready -[#D32F2F,bold]-> Implementing : <color:#D32F2F>request the implementation</color>
Implementing -[#888888]-> Checks : wait for the checks
Implementing -[#D32F2F,bold]-> Implementing : <color:#D32F2F>request the implementation again</color>
Implementing -[#888888]-> Decision : stop the implementation for the Owner
Checks -[#1565C0,bold]-> Reviewing : <color:#1565C0>request the review</color>
Checks -[#1565C0,bold]-> Implementing : <color:#1565C0>request a check fix</color>
Checks -[#888888]-> Decision : stop for failed checks
Checks -[#1565C0,bold]-> Implementing : <color:#1565C0>request a conflict resolution</color>
Checks -[#888888]-> Decision : stop for missing checks
Reviewing -[#1565C0,bold]-> Implementing : <color:#1565C0>request a review fix</color>
Reviewing -[#888888]-> Merging : start the merge
Reviewing -[#888888]-> OwnerReview : ask the Owner to decide the merge
Reviewing -[#D32F2F,bold]-> Reviewing : <color:#D32F2F>request the cause from the Reviewer</color>
Reviewing -[#888888]-> Decision : stop at the round limit
Reviewing -[#888888]-> Decision : stop the review for the Owner
Reviewing -[#888888]-> Checks : go back to the checks
Reviewing -[#D32F2F,bold]-> Reviewing : <color:#D32F2F>request the review again</color>
OwnerReview -[#888888]-> Merging : start the merge
OwnerReview -[#1565C0,bold]-> Implementing : <color:#1565C0>request a response to the Owner's review</color>
OwnerReview -[#1565C0,bold]-> Implementing : <color:#1565C0>request a conflict resolution</color>
OwnerReview -[#888888,dashed]-> Ready : the Owner adds ready
Merging -[#888888]-> [*] : close the merged issue
Merging -[#888888]-> Checks : go back to the checks
Merging -[#1565C0,bold]-> Implementing : <color:#1565C0>request a conflict resolution</color>
Merging -[#888888]-> Decision : stop the merge for the Owner
Decision -[#888888,dashed]-> Ready : the Owner adds ready

legend right
  <color:#D32F2F>**Red**</color>: cumin starts an agent, and reads the quota usage first. At a limit, cumin starts nothing
  and counts nothing; the issue keeps its state, and a later poll decides again.
  <color:#1565C0>**Blue**</color>: cumin starts an agent, and reads no usage: an issue in work goes on.
  Gray: cumin starts no agent (a label, a comment, a notification, a close). Dashed: the Owner acts.

  While cumin stops after the current runs (cumin stop --after-current-runs):
  cumin takes no red and no blue transition; the issue keeps its state until the next start.
  cumin still takes the gray transitions, and still sends a merge.
endlegend

@enduml
